 are hosted each week  happy hours discussions cooking classes  you name it even though the country is  still opening up and and states are  opening out people are still signing up  for the website connections like the one  fall between Pam and Sheldon I'm not  looking at what colors Sheldon is and  he's not looking at what color I am or  what color any of us so we're we're  human beings were in the same race and  let's make this world a better place  something we always talked about about  how we can make things better and how  everyone should be felt equal this is my  grandson this is somebody I'm proud of  and I want to be with for the rest of my  life so that's what quarantine buddy  gives you a virtual grandmother just one  possibility in our new socially distant  world for CBS this morning  Errol Barnett New York yes ma'am that is  what you want to see I like these are  pockets of sunshine I call them you know  good things happen to good people even  in the midst of this pain yeah well you  know we have an epidemic in this country  I think we also have an epidemic of  loneliness but that is alleviating it we  appreciate it  well done quarantine buddy
 

